cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MedIntelOS in academic or research work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "MedIntelOS: An Alpha-Stage Reference Implementation for Health-Data Interoperability, Clinical Decision Support, and Federated Learning"
authors:
  - family-names: "Plesca"
    given-names: "Ciprian Stefan"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-1340-0232"   # add if/when you register one — see note below
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ciprian-LocalPulse/MedIntelOS"
url: "https://agentflow-enterprise.com/"
abstract: >
  MedIntelOS is an open-source, alpha-stage reference implementation for
  experimenting with health-data interoperability (FHIR R5), clinical
  decision-support workflows (CDS Hooks), federated model aggregation,
  tamper-evident audit records, and patient-consent smart contracts. It is
  explicitly not a certified EHR, not a complete FHIR implementation, and not
  evidence of regulatory or clinical compliance — see the repository's own
  README and MEDICAL_DISCLAIMER.md for the current scope boundary.
keywords:
  - health-data-interoperability
  - fhir
  - cds-hooks
  - clinical-decision-support
  - federated-learning
  - zero-knowledge-proofs
license: MIT
version: "0.x-alpha"   # update to match the actual tag/release at time of citation
date-released: "2026-01-01"   # replace with the real date of the version being cited
